// SKILL.md (Types, Abstract): an abstract type "crosses data (json/toml/pack reads and
// writers, casts, `sys::net`) only through `impl Cast for T {};` ... (a method the impl
// leaves out uses the representation)". A cast OUT of an abstract value never crosses:
// the check accepts `cast<i64>(w)` and every run answers InvalidCast, with the impl or
// without it, while json::write_str of the same value writes the representation.
// run: timeout -s KILL 30 /home/eric/tmp/review-2026-11-16/bin/graphix --no-cache design/review-2026-11-16/repro/lang-skill-cast-out-of-abstract.gx
// expected (reading the skill): 1 {"W":1}
// observed: error:`InvalidCast("can't cast W(…) to i64: an abstract value has no primitive form") {"W":1}
type W = Abstract<i64>;
impl Cast for W {};
let v = W(1);
println("[cast<i64>(v)] [json::write_str(v)$]");
sys::exit(sys::time::after_idle(duration:100.ms, 0));
0
